From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:41:48 +0800
Subject: drm/msm/dp: Serialize HPD state updates

The plug and detect paths hold plugged_lock while accessing the sink
state, but IRQ-HPD processing updates the same state without that lock.
Unplug also changes the video-test flag and AUX transfer gate before
acquiring the lock.

Cover those updates with plugged_lock so that users of the connection
lock cannot observe partially updated HPD state. This also lets stream
failure cleanup decide whether to preserve AUX while excluding HPD
processing.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Reviewed-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Patchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/757251/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260930-msm-dp-hdr10-v1-4-dbbf8b2b42bc@radxa.com
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 62c6146e5fde2e47f051dd2aa29b99bc469349bf)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -558,6 +558,8 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 {
 	struct platform_device *pdev = dp->msm_dp_display.pdev;
 
+	guard(mutex)(&dp->plugged_lock);
+
 	dp->panel->video_test = false;
 
 	msm_dp_aux_enable_xfers(dp->aux, false);
@@ -566,7 +568,6 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 			dp->msm_dp_display.connector_type,
 			dp->link->sink_count);
 
-	guard(mutex)(&dp->plugged_lock);
 	if (!dp->plugged)
 		return 0;
 
@@ -608,6 +609,8 @@ static int msm_dp_irq_hpd_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 	u32 sink_request;
 	int rc = 0;
 
+	guard(mutex)(&dp->plugged_lock);
+
 	/* irq_hpd can happen at either connected or disconnected state */
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "Before, type=%d, sink_count=%d\n",
 			dp->msm_dp_display.connector_type,
-- 
